+# Line 1078: the marked passage and the complete released five-page block
+
+October 30, 2026. **The two previously unread middle pages locate the actual asterisked interpretation and complete our examination of this released five-page transcript block.** The marked row is labelled **1301:43 / Unknown**, on physical page 188 (printed page 3 of 5). The released block also contains two separately marked unintelligible passages and a qualifying footer. This improves the source trail behind the earlier request for a footnote. It does not validate the interpreted word, identify a voice, authenticate the original clock, or establish which version was delivered.
+
+The block has **48 timed rows, 45 distinct second labels and 22 separate minute markers**. These are counts of printed transcript fields, not calls, people, independent recordings or proven missing material. All earlier conflicting labels and dated assessments remain preserved.
+
+## Sources and reading scope
+
+The source is officially hosted released scan **AEA1130 / NARA 7598367**: [catalogue](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7598367), [exact PDF](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/4-UAL-175/e-Other/4-AEA-1130-COMPLETED-ACCID-PCKG--FORMAL-ACCID-PCKG-ZNY-ARTCC-148-UAL175-REDACT-SEALED.pdf). It was acquired in the [preceding study](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/e64f8f3006879bfde9fa76f1db4b9be6b514d5af/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-completed-package-original-2026-10-30/README.md), October 30, 2026: **15,505,493 bytes / 237 pages**, SHA-256 `5bb71c00b716fb59425571d0c714a97a32d84b13f35dcc65d7cc6bd6f83b5179`.
+
+No redownload occurred. The held entity's bytes, hash and page count were checked before rendering exactly two new images, physical **188 and 189**. Previously preserved images **186, 187 and 190** were reread. The first is the cover/first page and has no explicit printed “Page 1 of 5” label; the following images show pages 2, 3, 4 and 5 of 5. Our reading now covers all five physical pages 186–190 in this released block. Across this study and its predecessor, **18 distinct packet images have been read; 219 remain unread**.
+
+This is not whole-package reading, native Word authentication, historical signing/delivery authentication or source-audio completeness. Images were read before visible-raster OCR. No hidden PDF text extraction, redaction reconstruction, listening, waveform comparison, decoder work or clock fitting occurred. Raw PDF, rasters, full OCR, speech, personnel, signatures, contact, tracking, account and private-case material remain outside this public derivative.
+
+[SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json) records exact source and raster/OCR hashes, derivative line counts, new versus reused inputs, and predecessor reading limits. [FIELD-LEDGER.json](FIELD-LEDGER.json) records all 48 safe timestamp/agency rows, 22 minute markers, exact locators and preserved conflicts. Agency/notation joins are manual image readings; they are not inferred from OCR column order.
+
+## The actual uncertainty markings
+
+| Observation | Exact locator | What it establishes; what remains open |
+|---|---|---|
+| Asterisk before a parenthesized one-word interpretation; agency field “Unknown” | Physical 188 / printed 3 of 5; time at visible-OCR line 16; notation at line 58 | A marked interpretation exists at the printed second label 1301:43. The spoken word is excluded from this public payload. The original recording and check worksheet are needed to test its correctness. |
+| Separate unintelligible notation, N90 row | Physical 188; time 1301:28 at OCR 10; notation at OCR 50 | The transcript openly flags unclear content. This is a printed transcription judgment, not an independent measurement of noise, lost audio or the original speaker. |
+| Separate unintelligible notation, Unknown row | Physical 188; time 1301:46 at OCR 20; notation at OCR 60 | This is distinct from the asterisked interpretation. Do not merge the two uncertain passages into one event or count the notation as evidence of a covert participant. |
+| Asterisked footer and end label | Physical 190 / printed 5 of 5; OCR 34–35 and 37 | The footer says that the rerecording is not entirely clear and presents an interpretation as the best possible under the circumstances. This is the source's assessment. Its accuracy, review date and implementation history remain untested. |
+| Agency legend | Physical 186, above certification; first timed row at OCR 54 | The legend expands the code “Unknown” as “Unknown Agency.” It does not identify a person or establish intelligence affiliation. Manual image code AD1 remains distinct from the OCR's ADI reading. |
+
+The [earlier AEA1121 review list](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/a42d0956202dacc3b971d21f479966d56fefcd60/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-package-version-chain-2026-10-30/README.md), SHA-256 `71c0ecec8e0fa0a92bc27cfe28483733877b66c371ea732f12d5c5ad5c7905c6`, identifies the five-page Ninth transcript as TMU commercial phone line 1078 (physical 8, OCR 63–71). Its continuation requests the asterisked footnote under Order 8020.11B 77d(4) and displays “Change made” (physical 9, OCR 5–12). That earlier memo was already image-read; its safe fields are reused here.
+
+The [previously read 2000 policy](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/2e38da9806a4b3bc2550d66718831488aea76a6c/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-transcript-policy-crosswalk-2026-10-30/README.md), paragraph 77d(4), physical 60 / printed 324 / selected-text lines 32–37, describes conditional treatment of interpreted garbled words and unintelligible material. The [policy source](https://libraryonline.erau.edu/online-full-text/books-online/1177.pdf) has SHA-256 `4a079eef3618704785a50283ca6a28fb26be694191570a7f0b8549893ef8e3cf`.
+
+The released counterpart supplies an actual marked passage and footer, rather than only a reviewer's request. It does **not** prove that this is the exact version reviewed, that the annotation was added on a particular date, or that the interpretation complies with the original audio. The separate sector-55 “no footnote needed” response remains preserved for its different factual context; no comparison of its underlying recording is claimed here. Do not apply the later 2003 minute-grouping revision retroactively.
+
