+
+Manual image agency-code counts are **AD1: 21; N90: 20; Unknown: 2; AREA C OS: 2; AD2: 3**. These codes and counts do not identify 48 independent communications or a corresponding number of individuals. Exact printed body code “AREA C OS” and the cover legend's “Area COS” retain their typography; the earlier “Area C Sup” versus “Area C OS” query remains in its preserved source.
+
+Three second labels occur twice: **1301:07, 1303:39 and 1303:40**, each with an N90 and an AD1 row. Both rows are retained. Deduplicating by timestamp would discard three separately labelled rows. A shared printed second alone does not prove duplication, simultaneous speech, a splice or a bad clock.
+
+The header declares **1255–1316 UTC**, and every separate cardinal-minute label from 1255 through 1316 appears once in this released block. First and last timed speech-row labels are **1300:41 and 1310:14**. Nominal label arithmetic gives:
+
+- Header span: **1,260 seconds**.
+- Header start to first timed row: **341 seconds**.
+- First to last timed row: **573 seconds**.
+- Last timed row to header end: **346 seconds**.
+
+These values partition the written label span; they are **not measured recording durations, silence intervals, missing minutes or evidence of erased speech**. Minute markers and timed rows have different roles. Original recordings, channel/position mapping, clock source and transcription/check records remain necessary to evaluate actual coverage. This ground ATC line 1078 remains separate from the flight telephone/carrier/operator evidence track.
+
+## Conflicting released versions remain unresolved
+
+The [previously read two-page AWA937 entity](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/0584407dac2190a9f9514ee157124446e60672d5/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-tmu1078-source-2026-10-30/README.md), SHA-256 `a10386e4e39d455c7438328eca88bb28a76b7aea5c33282b4537779924851432`, and this block share January 17, 2002, the line 1078 position, the 1255–1316 range and first visible timestamp 1300:41. They retain conflicting fields:
+
+| Field | AWA937 | AEA1130, physical 186 |
+|---|---|---|
+| Aircraft subject | AAL11 | UAL175 |
+| Case addressee | ZBW-ARTCC-148 | ZNY-ARTCC-148 |
+| Certification subject | AAL11 | UAL175 |
+
+AWA937's `UAL175_R42_memo.doc` work-file label and `09/27/2001` footer token remain preserved. Neither source is selected as controlling. The five-page block's availability does not authenticate a common native origin or full-text/binary identity, explain the different labels, or establish an editing chronology. Template reuse, cross-incident assembly and version changes remain untested alternatives, not resolved explanations.
+
+Likewise, the outer packet's March 11, 2004 destruction label and the earlier retention directive remain as recorded in the preceding study. This unit supplies no new disposition authority, hold-withdrawal record or actual destruction finding.
+
+## Evidentiary strength, limits and next records
+
+The strongest new result is **source linkage**: the actual marked row can now be examined alongside the uncertainty footer and the earlier request. Visible qualifications are contrary evidence to a claim that this released version presents every word and agency as certain. They do not exclude other errors or establish an innocent or improper editing history.
+
+The decisive next inputs remain:
+
+1. Original line 1078 recording and identified rerecording generation, channel/time coverage and source-clock record; use the assigned technical owner for authorized technical comparison.
+2. Transcriber's/checker's existing worksheets and any timing-method remark, together with native Word versions and certification history.
+3. Exact January review enclosures, corrected versions, dispatch contents and recipient acknowledgment, rather than assuming the surviving archive copy was delivered.
+4. The remaining held OMIC, R42 and RA55 bodies and end pages; other selected fields still have incomplete reading scope.
+5. Actual May 2003 draft/corrected QFR and delivery acknowledgment; signed administrative action/no-action/reasons; distinct recommendation implementation/closure records. This 2002 transcript does not supply them.
+
+All five tracks and all eighteen substantive criteria remain open/partial. Native carrier/operator/call-leg/recipient/clock joins, recorder authenticated configuration/custody/paired output/clocks, materials specimen/native/calibration/same-specimen joins, and steel native preservation/transfer/inventory/attribution/selection inputs remain TODOs. Earlier technical tests are not duplicated or relabelled unperformed. No private correspondence, new request, outreach, fee, filing, private push, source overwrite, deletion, merge or history rewrite is part of this unit.
+
+## Verification and revision accountability
+
+[verify_fields.py](verify_fields.py) and [VERIFICATION.json](VERIFICATION.json) reproduce **24 passing scoped checks, zero failures**: the pinned whole-source entity, unchanged five image/OCR inputs, ordered timestamp and minute-marker ledgers, notation anchors, nominal arithmetic, and controls for a changed source or discarded rows. The machine checks timestamp columns; agency and notation-to-row joins remain manual image observations.
+
+The preceding study's **32 passes / four literal OCR failures remain unchanged**. Of/of, ADI/AD1 and S/5 are preserved as recognition observations; this different timestamp-ledger verifier neither repairs nor replaces those failed predicates. Do not combine the test counts into a historical-confidence score.
+
+To rerun with the preserved inputs, using Python 3.12.14 / pypdf 6.10.0:
+
+```sh
+python3 verify_fields.py --pdf /path/to/AEA1130.pdf \
+  --prior-media /path/to/faa-completed-package-original-2026-10-30 \
+  --new-media /path/to/faa-1078-marked-passages-2026-10-30
+```
+
+The input directories contain the pinned renders and visible OCR described in SOURCE-PINS. No raw source inputs are embedded in this public derivative. A successful rerun proves scoped field reproduction, not original voices, clock accuracy, semantic completeness, native signing, delivery, compliance, independence, intent or the five-track goal's completion.
+
